            "pk": "17950200089671747",
            "text": "Workshop Title: Crafting an Opening Speech for MUN Conference - Countering Emerging Cyber Threats in the Era of Artificial Intelligence\nDate: 28/04/2024\nTime: 14:00-15:20\nLocation: Aqtobe IT Hub, Abilkhairkhan street, 52a\n\n 🇺🇳Key Learning Objectives:\n\n🌐Understanding the Significance of the Opening Speech in MUN\n🌐Researching and Analyzing the Topic: Cyber Threats in the AI Era\n🌐Crafting a Compelling Narrative and Argument\n🌐Structuring Your Speech for Maximum Impact\n🌐Delivering with Confidence and Poise\n\nWho Should Attend:\n\nMUN Delegates of all Levels\nStudents Interested in International Relations and Cybersecurity\nThose Seeking to Enhance Their Public Speaking Skills\n\nWhy Attend?\nBy participating in this workshop, delegates will gain invaluable insights into the intricacies of crafting and delivering an effective opening speech for MUN conferences. Whether you’re a seasoned delegate or new to the MUN scene, this workshop will equip you with the tools and confidence needed to make a memorable impression and advocate for your country’s stance on countering cyber threats in the era of artificial intelligence.\n\n@laura_researcher \n@aqtobe.hub \n@inyaz__team \n@zhubanov.university"
